:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564492/2026-week-12-college-football-playoff-bowl-projections","type":"Story","byline":"Kyle Bonagura and Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Power Rankings: Chaos shifts top 25 in Week 12","description":"UCLA and Ohio State fell, and three teams joined the list. How did the top 25 change after a wild Week 12?","published":"2026-11-23T12:14:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870944/chris-peal","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Peal"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Peal","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Peal","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:45Z","intro":"Christopher Jenkins Jardru Peal (born March 27, 2005) is an American college football cornerback for the Syracuse Orange. He previously played for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Peal attended Providence Day School in Charlotte, North Carolina. During his high school career he had 123 tackles and three interceptions on defense and rushed 246 times for 1,919 yards and caught 48 passes for 556 yards with 36 total touchdowns on offense. He committed to University of Georgia to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Peal played in five games at Georgia in 2023 and 2024. After the 2024 season, he entered the transfer portal and transferred to Syracuse University. In his first year at Syracuse in 2025, he started all 12 games and recorded 43 tackles. Peal returned to Syracuse for the 2026 season."}]}}